  <!-- ================================ Command line ================================ -->
  <data name="CommandLineHelpTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Command line options</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CommandLineHelpBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>midi2monitor.exe [endpoint device id] [options]

  [endpoint device id]   Optional. The full endpoint device id of the device to
                         monitor. Wrap it in quotes if it contains spaces.

  --group, -g  number    Optional. The group number, 1 through 16, to monitor.
                         Only valid when an endpoint device id is supplied.

  --channel, -c number   Optional. The channel number, 1 through 16, to monitor.
                         Only valid when a group is also supplied.

  --simple, --advanced   Optional. Open in simple or advanced mode, for this window
                         only. Without either, the mode you used last is used.
                         An endpoint supplied in advanced mode is watched without
                         changing your saved sources.

  --help, -h, -?         Show this help.

Examples

  midi2monitor.exe
  midi2monitor.exe "\\?\SWD#MIDISRV#MIDIU_DIAG_LOOPBACK_A#{e7cce071-3c03-423f-88d3-f1045d02552b}"
  midi2monitor.exe "\\?\SWD#MIDISRV#..." --group 1 --channel 10
  midi2monitor.exe --advanced</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CommandLineErrorTitle" xml:space="preserve">
